ale","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10755","person_slug":"richard-di-natale","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ricky Muir","party":"Australian Motoring Enthusiast Party","person_id":"tvfy_10834","person_slug":"ricky-muir","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Robert Simms","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10842","person_slug":"robert-simms","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sam Dastyari","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10819","person_slug":"sam-dastyari","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"no"},{"name":"Scott Ludlam","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10713","person_slug":"scott-ludlam","vote":"no"},{"name":"Scott Ryan","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10715","person_slug":"scott-ryan","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sean Edwards","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10756","person_slug":"sean-edwards","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Simon Birmingham","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10044","person_slug":"simon-birmingham","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Stephen Parry","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10507","person_slug":"stephen-parry","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Zed Seselja","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10822","person_slug":"zed-seselja","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Motions - East West Link - Re-allocate funds","noes":29,"question":"The majority voted in favour of a [motion](http://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?id=2015-11-25.136.2) introduced by Australian Motoring Enthusiast Party [Senator Ricky Muir](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/victoria/ricky_muir), which means the motion was successful. The motion asked that the funds currently set aside for the [East West Link](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_West_Link_%28Melbourne%29) in Victoria be re-allocated. Read more on [ABC News](http://www.abc.net.au/news/2015-04-15/victorian-government-to-pay-339-million-east-west-link-contracts/6393536) about why the East West Link hasn't gone ahead yet and doesn't look like it will for the foreseeable future. ### Motion text > *That the Senate—* > *(a) notes that:* >> *(i) there is a political stalemate between the Federal Government and the Victorian State Government in relation to the [East West Link](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_West_Link_%28Melbourne%29),* >> *(ii) there is approximately $1.5 billion in unspent allocations to the East West Link,* >> *(iii) evidence presented to the Rural and Regional Affairs and Transport References Committee [inquiry into aspects of road safety](http://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Committees/Senate/Rural_and_Regional_Affairs_and_Transport/Road_safety) in Australia by the [National Rural Health Alliance](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Rural_Health_Alliance) demonstrated that those who live outside the major cities make up 30 per cent of the population and 52 per cent of deaths due to land transport accidents,* >> *(iv) rural roads play a vital role in putting food on city tables and bringing resources to urban areas,* >> *(v) the annual economic cost of road crashes in Australia is enormous – estimated at $27 billion per annum – and the social impacts are devastating,* >> *(vi) many rural roads are in dangerously poor condition and in desperate need of repair,* >> *(vii) some local councils in Victoria do not have the necessary fu","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-3995","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2015-11-25/2"}
